  "stem": "The function \\(f\\) is defined by \\(f(x) = 4(x - 3) + 10\\). What is the \\(y\\)-intercept of the graph of \\(y = f(x)\\) in the \\(xy\\)-plane?",
  "figure": null,
  "answer_type": "mcq",
  "choices": {
    "A": "\\((0, -2)\\)",
    "B": "\\((0, 10)\\)",
    "C": "\\((0, -12)\\)",
    "D": "\\((0, 2)\\)"
  },
  "answer": "A",
  "spr_answers": null,
  "solution": [
    "The \\(y\\)-intercept is the point \\((0, f(0))\\).",
    "\\(f(0) = 4(0 - 3) + 10 = -12 + 10 = -2\\), so the \\(y\\)-intercept is \\((0, -2)\\).",
    "Equivalently, expand: \\(f(x) = 4x - 12 + 10 = 4x - 2\\)."
  ],
  "explanation": {
    "A": "Correct. \\(f(0) = 4(0 - 3) + 10 = -12 + 10 = -2\\).",
    "B": "Incorrect. 10 is the constant written at the end, but the \\(y\\)-intercept is \\(f(0)\\), and \\(4(0 - 3)\\) also contributes.",
    "C": "Incorrect. This is \\(4(0 - 3)\\) without adding 10.",
    "D": "Incorrect. \\(f(0) = -12 + 10 = -2\\), not \\(12 - 10\\)."
  },
  "traps": {
    "B": "stopped_early",
    "C": "arithmetic",
    "D": "sign_error"
  },
